cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you discuss Ballarch, please cite it as below.
  Text and diagrams are licensed under CC BY 4.0 (see NOTICE.md); the code
  in this repository has no software license yet.
title: "Ballarch Core 2.0: owners, obligations and honest outcomes (specification and reference implementations)"
abstract: >-
  Ballarch is an architecture for components that own state and call systems
  that can fail, from hardware blocks and firmware to mobile apps, services,
  workflows and AI-agent tools. Each piece of mutable state that Ballarch
  governs has one owner that decides in pure functions. A runtime commits each
  decision atomically before anything leaves, and gives every outbound call
  exactly one outcome: Done, NotDone or Unknown. The outcome follows from two
  boundaries in time, the commit and send horizons, and from the effect class
  declared for the port: Safe, Idempotent or NonIdempotent. A timeout after an
  effectful request may have been sent is never reported as NotDone without
  evidence. The runtime, not feature code, owns retries, idempotency keys,
  crash recovery and optional reconciliation. It derives a key for every call,
  ties repeats to intents, refuses deadlines that outlive a declared
  deduplication window, and, under the Durable profile, holds its store
  exclusively. A knowledge algebra over Kleene's three-valued logic bounds
  what an operation of several calls may claim, so that a settled composite
  can answer its caller like one honest call, given honest adapters, absorbing
  compensations and a durable call ledger. The distribution contains the
  specification; reference implementations in Kotlin, C and SystemVerilog,
  which check the outcome rules and the knowledge algebra at each level
  separately (composition across levels is not tested); an Alloy model of the
  call protocol; a language-neutral conformance-trace checker; and an agent
  skill. Ballarch costs a runtime dependency, explicit stages and, under the
  Durable profile, at least three durable writes per effectful call.
version: 2.0.0-rc.1
type: software
